<score-partwise version="4.0">
  <work>
    <work-title>The Second Booke of Songs or Ayres — II. Lachrimæ ("Flow my teares")</work-title>
  </work>
  <movement-title>Complete song (one stanza of music, 24 bars); Canto, Basso and lute tablature</movement-title>
  <identification>
    <creator type="composer">John Dowland</creator>
    <rights>Transcription released under CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication). The underlying composition is in the public domain.</rights>
    <encoding>
      <software>public-domain-scores tools/export.py</software>
      <encoding-date>2026-10-06</encoding-date>
    </encoding>
    <source>John Dowland, The Second Booke of Songs or Ayres, London: Thomas Este for George Eastland, 1600, song II (Boston Public Library copy G.400.52, Internet Archive secondbookeofson00dowl), leaves n13 (Canto with French lute tablature) and n14 (Basso, printed rotated; last Canto/lute line). Lute part = sounding pitches decoded from the tablature (tenor G tuning, 7th course D).</source>
  </identification>
